<title>USA: General Chemical buys stock held by Stonor.</title>
<headline>General Chemical buys stock held by Stonor.</headline>
<dateline>HAMPTON, N.H. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Chemical Group Inc said it repurchased for $27 million, or about $20.10 each, 1.34 million shares in the company owned by Stonor Group Ltd of Liberia.</p>
<p>Stonor also sold its remaining 3.1 million shares in General Chemical to an investor group including Gildea Management Co and Equitable Life Assurance Society of Britain, both of which now own more than five percent of the common stock.</p>
<p>General Chemical stock was 1/2 firmer at 22-1/2 in late morning trade. ((-- New York Newsrom 212 859 1610))</p>
